1
00:01:31,092 --> 00:01:32,093
[faint beep]

2
00:01:34,929 --> 00:01:37,098
[electronic buzzing, static]

3
00:01:49,068 --> 00:01:51,320
[machinery powering up]

4
00:01:56,409 --> 00:01:58,411
[♪ Ominous music playing]

5
00:02:19,682 --> 00:02:21,309
[electronics whirring]

6
00:02:36,282 --> 00:02:37,283
[muffled rumbling]

7
00:02:38,034 --> 00:02:39,035
[muffled clanging]

8
00:02:52,381 --> 00:02:53,966
[boosters roaring]

9
00:03:03,434 --> 00:03:04,852
[loud clanging]

10
00:03:07,313 --> 00:03:08,522
[chains clanking]

11
00:03:17,865 --> 00:03:19,325
[heavy thud]

12
00:03:23,245 --> 00:03:24,580
[high-pitched
metallic ringing]

13
00:03:24,747 --> 00:03:25,873
[crackling]

14
00:03:38,719 --> 00:03:40,554
[metal groaning]

15
00:03:48,062 --> 00:03:49,605
[lever buzzing]

16
00:03:59,740 --> 00:04:01,367
[♪ Ominous music soars]

17
00:04:04,370 --> 00:04:05,579
[♪ Music subsides]

18
00:04:09,375 --> 00:04:11,377
[♪ Uneasy music playing]

19
00:04:21,011 --> 00:04:23,013
[♪ Ominous
choral music playing]

20
00:04:44,118 --> 00:04:45,119
[♪ Music fades]

21
00:05:09,268 --> 00:05:11,479
[faint ringing]

22
00:05:14,148 --> 00:05:16,901
[alarm blaring]

23
00:05:18,027 --> 00:05:19,028
[sighs softly]

24
00:05:19,195 --> 00:05:20,613
[announcer over PA]
<i>Attention all workers.</i>

25
00:05:20,696 --> 00:05:22,406
<i>Attention all workers.</i>

26
00:05:22,573 --> 00:05:25,701
<i>Day shift starting
in T-minus 15 minutes.</i>

27
00:05:25,868 --> 00:05:28,496
<i>Farmers to report
to mess hall immediately.</i>

28
00:05:29,413 --> 00:05:31,207
<i>If you are experiencing
any symptoms,</i>

29
00:05:31,290 --> 00:05:32,666
<i>such as fever, cough,</i>

30
00:05:32,833 --> 00:05:34,752
<i>vomiting,
or difficulty breathing,</i>

31
00:05:34,919 --> 00:05:37,338
<i>proceed to the medical bay
for examination.</i>

32
00:05:37,505 --> 00:05:38,756
- [thunder rumbles]
- [rain pattering]

33
00:05:38,923 --> 00:05:41,008
<i>The safety and well-being
of our colony</i>

34
00:05:41,091 --> 00:05:43,886
<i>is Weyland-Yutani's
top priority.</i>

35
00:05:44,720 --> 00:05:46,430
<i>Attention all workers...</i>

36
00:05:46,597 --> 00:05:49,475
[man] <i>Did you hear about
the claustrophobic astronaut?</i>

37
00:05:50,059 --> 00:05:51,060
<i>He needed space.</i>

38
00:05:51,227 --> 00:05:52,937
[woman] I'm begging you,
you got to stop.

39
00:05:53,103 --> 00:05:56,649
I just spent my full share
on a belt that won't fit.

40
00:05:57,107 --> 00:05:58,359
Huge waist.

41
00:05:58,567 --> 00:05:59,610
See that cornbread.

42
00:06:02,196 --> 00:06:04,573
[sputters] Maybe it's 'cause
I'm on this seafood diet.

43
00:06:05,115 --> 00:06:06,951
I see food, I eat it.

44
00:06:08,369 --> 00:06:09,787
That's so bad.

45
00:06:09,954 --> 00:06:11,372
You always laughed
at that one.

46
00:06:11,539 --> 00:06:12,998
Yeah, when I was 12.

47
00:06:13,499 --> 00:06:14,708
[device ringing]

48
00:06:17,711 --> 00:06:19,338
I'm sure it's Mr. Finch.

49
00:06:20,339 --> 00:06:21,966
We owe him three months today.

50
00:06:23,300 --> 00:06:24,677
He'll call again.

51
00:06:26,178 --> 00:06:29,848
Well, maybe we won't be here
when he does.

52
00:06:30,099 --> 00:06:31,934
[indistinct chatter]

53
00:06:37,022 --> 00:06:38,941
[woman] Andy.
Stay close to me.

54
00:06:41,902 --> 00:06:44,321
[revolutionist over speakers]
<i>Wake up. Wake up now.</i>

55
00:06:45,072 --> 00:06:47,449
<i>We're all
Weyland-Yutani slaves.</i>

56
00:06:47,616 --> 00:06:49,994
<i>The company pays us
with food and shelter</i>

57
00:06:50,119 --> 00:06:53,163
<i>and takes our lives
in exchange.</i>

58
00:06:53,289 --> 00:06:55,374
<i>Don't believe their lies.</i>

59
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:57,501
<i>They own you!</i>

60
00:06:58,294 --> 00:06:59,837
[woman] Andy, Andy.
Hey, hey, hey.

61
00:07:00,004 --> 00:07:01,338
Hey, Andy. Come on. Come on.

62
00:07:03,215 --> 00:07:05,217
- What did I do?
- It's a scam.

63
00:07:05,384 --> 00:07:06,969
The ball is never under
the cup that you pick.

64
00:07:07,136 --> 00:07:08,137
It's a trick.

65
00:07:08,304 --> 00:07:10,514
But how am I
gonna get the money?

66
00:07:10,889 --> 00:07:11,890
Money for what?

67
00:07:12,057 --> 00:07:15,853
To pay for the horse
when we get to Yvaga.

68
00:07:16,020 --> 00:07:17,771
You're gonna get a horse?

69
00:07:17,938 --> 00:07:20,441
I wanna call it Raindy.

70
00:07:21,650 --> 00:07:23,235
Do you get it?

71
00:07:24,069 --> 00:07:25,613
- Raindy.
- No, I like it.

72
00:07:25,696 --> 00:07:27,364
Yeah, it's good.

73
00:07:28,741 --> 00:07:31,535
Okay, so you just
wait over there.

74
00:07:31,702 --> 00:07:32,911
Okay, I might be a minute.

75
00:07:34,538 --> 00:07:36,040
Stay out of trouble,
all right?

76
00:07:36,206 --> 00:07:39,001
[announcer over PA]
<i>All employees will be seen.</i>

77
00:07:39,168 --> 00:07:40,336
[Andy] Good luck.

78
00:07:40,502 --> 00:07:42,713
[announcer over PA]
<i>Line up in an orderly fashion.</i>

79
00:07:42,880 --> 00:07:44,173
[officer over PA] <i>Next.</i>

80
00:07:44,340 --> 00:07:46,133
<i>Full name
and occupation, please.</i>

81
00:07:46,300 --> 00:07:49,553
<i>Marie Raines Carradine, ma'am.
Farming.</i>

82
00:07:49,720 --> 00:07:50,929
It's about my travel papers.

83
00:07:52,014 --> 00:07:54,600
<i>I met my quota, and I should
be free to go now.</i>

84
00:07:55,017 --> 00:07:56,060
Right?

85
00:07:56,226 --> 00:07:57,436
[officer] Go where?

86
00:07:57,603 --> 00:07:58,771
<i>Yvaga.</i>

87
00:07:59,396 --> 00:08:02,399
<i>It's an independent system,
but it's fully terraformed.</i>

88
00:08:03,567 --> 00:08:05,486
<i>You can actually see
the sun out there.</i>

89
00:08:05,653 --> 00:08:07,029
<i>Where are your parents?</i>

90
00:08:08,197 --> 00:08:11,158
<i>Uh, they died
three cycles ago.</i>

91
00:08:11,617 --> 00:08:13,369
Lung disease, from the mines.

92
00:08:14,286 --> 00:08:15,829
<i>It's just me
and my brother now.</i>

93
00:08:16,997 --> 00:08:18,165
[revolutionist over speakers]
<i>They sell us hope</i>

94
00:08:18,248 --> 00:08:19,541
<i>to keep us slaves.</i>

95
00:08:20,250 --> 00:08:25,923
<i>They sell us hope to keep
us slaves. Wake up now.</i>

96
00:08:30,678 --> 00:08:32,221
[indistinct chatter]

97
00:08:34,264 --> 00:08:35,641
[laughter]

98
00:08:37,226 --> 00:08:38,811
[officer] I'm sorry,
but you're not eligible

99
00:08:38,894 --> 00:08:40,104
for contract release yet.

100
00:08:40,270 --> 00:08:41,313
Due to a shortage of workers,

101
00:08:41,397 --> 00:08:42,773
you're being
transferred to the mines.

102
00:08:42,940 --> 00:08:44,233
<i>Wait, what?</i>

103
00:08:44,858 --> 00:08:46,902
<i>No, no, no,
I reached the required hours.</i>

104
00:08:47,069 --> 00:08:48,320
You have to let me go.

105
00:08:48,445 --> 00:08:51,323
Unfortunately, quotas have
been raised to 24,000 hours,

106
00:08:51,490 --> 00:08:52,991
so you'll be released
from contract

107
00:08:53,075 --> 00:08:54,284
in another five to six years.

108
00:08:54,451 --> 00:08:56,412
Thank you, and remember
the company is really grateful

109
00:08:56,578 --> 00:08:57,788
for your ongoing service.

110
00:08:58,122 --> 00:09:00,249
- [Andy] Rain!
- [Rain] Hey!

111
00:09:00,416 --> 00:09:01,500
Hey, stop!

112
00:09:01,667 --> 00:09:03,711
Get off him! You bastards!

113
00:09:05,587 --> 00:09:07,339
- [whimpering]
- I got you, I got you.

114
00:09:07,506 --> 00:09:08,757
Oh, shit, you're bleeding.

115
00:09:11,552 --> 00:09:12,594
Okay.

116
00:09:13,929 --> 00:09:16,181
- [device beeps, cranking]
- [Rain] You're okay.

117
00:09:16,348 --> 00:09:17,683
I'm resetting you.

118
00:09:18,016 --> 00:09:19,017
I got you.

119
00:09:19,685 --> 00:09:20,769
[gasps]

120
00:09:21,645 --> 00:09:22,813
It's okay.

121
00:09:22,980 --> 00:09:24,398
I shouldn't
have left you alone.

122
00:09:29,945 --> 00:09:31,363
[revolutionist over speakers]
<i>They sell us hope</i>

123
00:09:31,447 --> 00:09:33,449
<i>to keep us slaves.</i>

124
00:09:33,615 --> 00:09:35,659
<i>Wake up now. They own you.</i>

125
00:09:36,827 --> 00:09:38,871
[comms ringing]

126
00:09:38,954 --> 00:09:39,955
[Tyler over comms] <i>Hi, Rain.</i>

127
00:09:40,122 --> 00:09:41,623
<i>Look, I'm sorry. I know
I've been calling you all day,</i>

128
00:09:41,790 --> 00:09:43,375
<i>but, look,
something's come up,</i>

129
00:09:43,459 --> 00:09:44,877
<i>and I think you should
know about it.</i>

130
00:09:45,043 --> 00:09:47,588
<i>So, come by the trailers
and bring Andy.</i>

131
00:09:56,263 --> 00:09:58,974
[machinery thudding
and clanking]

132
00:10:09,276 --> 00:10:10,694
[indistinct conversation]

133
00:10:17,910 --> 00:10:18,911
Hey.

134
00:10:19,995 --> 00:10:21,038
[man] Oh, for...

135
00:10:21,205 --> 00:10:22,623
[automated voice over gaming
console] <i>Game over, man.</i>

136
00:10:23,165 --> 00:10:25,709
Sup, Rain? Long time no see.

137
00:10:26,084 --> 00:10:27,669
I told you she'd show up.

138
00:10:28,420 --> 00:10:29,630
You owe me five bucks.

139
00:10:30,839 --> 00:10:31,965
[man 2] <i>Andy!</i>

140
00:10:32,633 --> 00:10:34,134
[door opens, whirring]

141
00:10:34,885 --> 00:10:36,929
Why'd the blind miner
fall down the well?

142
00:10:37,095 --> 00:10:38,430
Why?

143
00:10:40,349 --> 00:10:41,433
'Cause he couldn't see
that well.

144
00:10:42,643 --> 00:10:43,977
Please don't encourage him.

145
00:10:44,728 --> 00:10:46,647
All right, go inside.
I'll be there in a second.

146
00:10:52,694 --> 00:10:53,987
- Kay.
- Rain.

147
00:10:54,154 --> 00:10:55,197
- Hi.
- Hi!

148
00:10:55,364 --> 00:10:56,448
Hi.

149
00:10:57,366 --> 00:10:59,159
[Kay] I missed you.

150
00:10:59,326 --> 00:11:01,161
And I know my brother
missed you, too.

151
00:11:05,874 --> 00:11:07,751
I'm really glad you came.

152
00:11:09,211 --> 00:11:11,255
[Rain] I heard about your dad.

153
00:11:11,421 --> 00:11:12,422
I'm really sorry.

154
00:11:13,215 --> 00:11:15,175
Well, between the hailstorms

155
00:11:15,259 --> 00:11:16,468
and the new diseases
every cycle...

156
00:11:16,635 --> 00:11:18,178
Yeah, everybody's dying,
right?

157
00:11:18,387 --> 00:11:20,013
So, should we show her?

158
00:11:20,514 --> 00:11:21,890
Show me what?

159
00:11:22,182 --> 00:11:25,143
- [system beeps]
- Okay, so, last night,

160
00:11:25,227 --> 00:11:26,645
we're loading up
the last Tesotek,

161
00:11:26,812 --> 00:11:28,313
we're about 200 miles
above the ground,

162
00:11:28,397 --> 00:11:29,398
and then all of a sudden...

163
00:11:29,565 --> 00:11:30,774
[imitates rapid beeping]

164
00:11:31,275 --> 00:11:32,651
The hauler picks up
this beacon.

165
00:11:32,818 --> 00:11:34,820
So Navarro tracks it,
and it turns out

166
00:11:34,987 --> 00:11:36,280
there's this big Wey-Yu ship

167
00:11:36,363 --> 00:11:37,781
drifting
right above our heads.

168
00:11:37,948 --> 00:11:38,949
Drifting?

169
00:11:39,116 --> 00:11:40,742
Decommissioned. Abandoned.

170
00:11:40,909 --> 00:11:42,870
Some old relic. It's probably
damaged or obsolete.

171
00:11:43,036 --> 00:11:44,246
Like that guy over there.

172
00:11:44,413 --> 00:11:45,414
[Navarro] Bjorn.

173
00:11:46,748 --> 00:11:48,959
Okay, just tell her.

174
00:11:49,126 --> 00:11:50,711
Why are we all
sitting around here

175
00:11:50,878 --> 00:11:52,421
waiting for travel permits
that the company

176
00:11:52,546 --> 00:11:54,214
are never gonna give to us?

177
00:11:54,673 --> 00:11:55,716
'Cause that hauler
has enough power in it

178
00:11:55,799 --> 00:11:56,800
to get us to Yvaga.

179
00:11:56,967 --> 00:11:59,761
Because it takes nine years
to get to Yvaga

180
00:11:59,928 --> 00:12:02,014
and you can't make that trip
without cryo-sleep.

181
00:12:02,180 --> 00:12:03,515
Decommissioned ships
still carry

182
00:12:03,599 --> 00:12:04,766
tons of functional equipment.

183
00:12:04,933 --> 00:12:06,393
And the hyperlink shows

184
00:12:06,476 --> 00:12:08,270
that ship
still has a few pods left.

185
00:12:10,397 --> 00:12:11,398
[chuckles in disbelief]

186
00:12:12,107 --> 00:12:15,485
You want to break into
a Weyland-Yutani ship

187
00:12:15,569 --> 00:12:17,905
and steal highly
regulated equipment?

188
00:12:18,071 --> 00:12:19,281
Before someone else does.

189
00:12:19,448 --> 00:12:20,449
[laughs]

190
00:12:21,199 --> 00:12:22,409
You guys are insane.

191
00:12:22,576 --> 00:12:23,702
- Well, of course we are.
- [man] No. No, we're not.

192
00:12:23,869 --> 00:12:25,078
- This is...
- [Navarro] That's what I said.

193
00:12:25,245 --> 00:12:26,455
[Kay] Are you gonna help us?

194
00:12:28,874 --> 00:12:30,667
[hesitates] Sorry,
what do you need me for?

195
00:12:32,836 --> 00:12:33,837
Andy.

196
00:12:34,254 --> 00:12:35,923
- We need to use Andy.
- Andy?

197
00:12:36,089 --> 00:12:37,090
[Bjorn] Mm-hmm.

198
00:12:37,257 --> 00:12:39,843
[man] He's a Weyland-Yutani
synthetic. He speaks Mother.

199
00:12:40,010 --> 00:12:41,428
He can access
a terminal on the ship

200
00:12:41,511 --> 00:12:42,971
to get us in and out
without a fuss.

201
00:12:43,138 --> 00:12:44,389
It's the only way to get in.

202
00:12:44,556 --> 00:12:46,642
Okay,
but what if we get caught?

203
00:12:46,808 --> 00:12:49,269
It'll ruin our chances of ever
getting a travel permit.

204
00:12:49,436 --> 00:12:50,979
Right, Rain's not comin'.

205
00:12:51,146 --> 00:12:53,398
Uh, how about you let us
take Andy then?

206
00:12:54,191 --> 00:12:56,568
I'm not sending
my brother up there alone.

207
00:12:57,319 --> 00:12:58,445
He's not your
brother though, is he?

208
00:12:58,612 --> 00:13:00,656
- Bjorn, shut the fuck up.
- It's true, though, isn't it?

209
00:13:00,822 --> 00:13:02,074
He's not your brother.
It's just Wey-Yu damaged goods

210
00:13:02,240 --> 00:13:03,700
that your dad
found in the trash.

211
00:13:03,867 --> 00:13:05,786
And that's all he is, Rain.
So just wake up.

212
00:13:06,453 --> 00:13:07,496
Let's go.

213
00:13:07,579 --> 00:13:08,664
- [Andy] Rain?
- [Bjorn] What?

214
00:13:08,747 --> 00:13:10,874
- I didn't say anything.
- [man] Rain, wait.

215
00:13:11,667 --> 00:13:12,668
I'm sorry.
Listen, I know my cousin

216
00:13:12,793 --> 00:13:13,794
can be a dick sometimes,
all right?

217
00:13:13,961 --> 00:13:15,629
But he is right
about something.

218
00:13:16,338 --> 00:13:17,339
You need to wake up.

219
00:13:17,756 --> 00:13:18,757
Because this company,

220
00:13:18,840 --> 00:13:19,841
they're not gonna
give us anything.

221
00:13:20,008 --> 00:13:22,010
You know that as well as I do.
We have to take it.

222
00:13:22,177 --> 00:13:24,179
[♪ Somber music playing]

223
00:13:26,223 --> 00:13:27,265
Rain, I just...

224
00:13:28,058 --> 00:13:29,810
I don't want to end up
like our parents.

225
00:13:30,560 --> 00:13:31,770
Do you?

226
00:13:33,230 --> 00:13:34,314
[bird chirping]

227
00:13:36,817 --> 00:13:40,320
Is it as easy as you're making
it sound, this plan of yours?

228
00:13:41,321 --> 00:13:43,240
You won't even have to get out
of the <i>Corbelan.</i>

229
00:13:43,657 --> 00:13:45,367
That much
I can promise you, okay?

230
00:13:49,496 --> 00:13:50,956
Come on. What do you say?

231
00:13:52,833 --> 00:13:54,543
[engines powering up]

232
00:14:04,386 --> 00:14:05,804
[thunder rumbles]

233
00:14:15,313 --> 00:14:16,857
[man] Bjorn, hurry up,
let's go.

234
00:14:21,028 --> 00:14:23,905
All right, I'm starting
her up. Batteries on.

235
00:14:26,408 --> 00:14:27,409
- [Bjorn] Lovely.
- [system powering up]

236
00:14:29,202 --> 00:14:30,495
[Navarro] Could I get hydro,
please?

237
00:14:31,663 --> 00:14:32,664
Comm panel.

238
00:14:34,666 --> 00:14:35,709
Ground spoilers.

239
00:14:35,876 --> 00:14:36,960
[man] They are armed.

240
00:14:37,919 --> 00:14:39,046
[Bjorn] First time
in space, huh?

241
00:14:39,212 --> 00:14:40,213
[Rain] Yeah.

242
00:14:41,506 --> 00:14:43,341
[Bjorn] You too? Boop!

243
00:14:43,925 --> 00:14:45,927
- [Navarro] Fuel pump.
- [man] On.

244
00:14:46,011 --> 00:14:47,012
[Bjorn] Two space virgins
coming through.

245
00:14:47,345 --> 00:14:49,514
[man] Right, take a good look
outside the window

246
00:14:49,681 --> 00:14:51,767
'cause the way I see it,
we're never coming back.

247
00:14:52,434 --> 00:14:53,935
[engines roaring]

248
00:15:00,150 --> 00:15:02,736
[praying in Mandarin]

249
00:15:05,155 --> 00:15:06,198
[in English] You good?

250
00:15:06,364 --> 00:15:07,365
