Nah, we're not fuckin' leavin'
her, okay? You understand?

754
00:44:17,364 --> 00:44:19,491
Then have mercy
and end her life now.

755
00:44:20,075 --> 00:44:22,786
If not, you all die.

756
00:44:24,913 --> 00:44:26,456
[Bjorn] So what the fuck
is he ea yin'?

757
00:44:26,623 --> 00:44:27,874
What's it doing to her?

758
00:44:28,041 --> 00:44:29,167
The parasitoid is implanting

759
00:44:29,251 --> 00:44:30,794
the Plagiarus Praepotens
in her.

760
00:44:30,961 --> 00:44:32,128
I beg your pardon?

761
00:44:32,295 --> 00:44:35,006
A seed that will amalgamate
with her DNA

762
00:44:35,090 --> 00:44:36,341
and rapidly grow out of her.

763
00:44:36,508 --> 00:44:37,926
What's gonna grow out of her?

764
00:44:40,720 --> 00:44:42,472
[♪ Dramatic music playing]

765
00:44:49,646 --> 00:44:52,440
XX121 Xenomorph.

766
00:44:53,316 --> 00:44:54,442
One of our towing ships

767
00:44:54,526 --> 00:44:57,904
first made contact with this
specimen two decades ago.

768
00:44:58,071 --> 00:44:59,281
Of the seven crew members

769
00:44:59,364 --> 00:45:01,408
aboard the <i>USS Nostromo,</i>
only one survived,

770
00:45:01,575 --> 00:45:03,618
blowing the creature
out of the airlock.

771
00:45:04,411 --> 00:45:06,580
We've been searching
for it ever since.

772
00:45:07,289 --> 00:45:10,542
170 days ago,
our search came to an end

773
00:45:10,709 --> 00:45:12,752
and the body of the Xenomorph
was brought on board...

774
00:45:13,420 --> 00:45:14,921
presumed dead.

775
00:45:15,088 --> 00:45:16,381
But of course,

776
00:45:16,548 --> 00:45:20,385
lack of oxygen and food is
of no true consequence to this

777
00:45:20,552 --> 00:45:21,970
perfect organism.

778
00:45:22,137 --> 00:45:24,139
Yet nothing is truly immortal.

779
00:45:25,891 --> 00:45:26,933
Clearly.

780
00:45:27,434 --> 00:45:30,145
It wreaked havoc
over this station,

781
00:45:30,812 --> 00:45:33,398
