1513
01:35:09,621 --> 01:35:10,789
<i>five,</i>

1514
01:35:10,956 --> 01:35:12,499
- <i>four, three...</i>
- Come on.

1515
01:35:13,458 --> 01:35:15,335
<i>...two, one.</i>

1516
01:35:21,174 --> 01:35:22,175
[Rain] Kay.

1517
01:35:24,386 --> 01:35:25,554
[panting]

1518
01:35:26,930 --> 01:35:28,390
What took you so long?

1519
01:35:28,557 --> 01:35:29,766
Let's get you outta here.

1520
01:35:31,184 --> 01:35:33,061
<i>I'm glad to see
you two made it.</i>

1521
01:35:53,081 --> 01:35:54,833
[boosters roaring]

1522
01:36:02,716 --> 01:36:04,468
[metal groaning]

1523
01:36:31,495 --> 01:36:32,704
[Rain] I got you.
Watch your head.

1524
01:36:34,706 --> 01:36:37,000
- Thank you.
- You're gonna be just fine.

1525
01:36:37,918 --> 01:36:39,002
Both of you.

1526
01:36:48,762 --> 01:36:50,722
<i>The company
couldn't be prouder</i>

1527
01:36:50,806 --> 01:36:52,057
<i>of what's been
accomplished here today.</i>

1528
01:36:52,975 --> 01:36:54,893
<i>I've sent
a message back to HQ.</i>

1529
01:36:55,060 --> 01:36:56,228
<i>When received in six months,</i>

1530
01:36:56,311 --> 01:36:57,396
<i>they'll travel
to Jackson's Star</i>

1531
01:36:57,562 --> 01:36:59,481
<i>to retrieve the compound from
you for further development.</i>

1532
01:37:06,321 --> 01:37:07,406
<i>What are you doing?</i>

1533
01:37:08,699 --> 01:37:10,117
Change of plans.

1534
01:37:12,327 --> 01:37:14,246
<i>Andy, stop her.</i>

1535
01:37:14,788 --> 01:37:16,123
<i>Reconnect us now.</i>

1536
01:37:19,042 --> 01:37:20,752
<i>No, no, no.
You two cannot do this.</i>

1537
01:37:20,919 --> 01:37:22,379
<i>The compound must be delivered
to the company.</i>

1538
01:37:23,171 --> 01:37:25,173
<i>I'm afraid
I must deny your petition.</i>

1539
01:37:25,549 --> 01:37:27,551
- <i>Have a nice day.</i>
- [static]

1540
01:37:27,634 --> 01:37:29,970
Now you better listen to me
here, now, you two.

1541
01:37:30,137 --> 01:37:33,098
You are insignificant in the
great scheme of things. You...

1542
01:37:34,433 --> 01:37:35,767
[station rumbling]

1543
01:37:39,938 --> 01:37:40,939
No.

1544
01:37:56,288 --> 01:37:58,999
This will keep your systems
online until we get to Yvaga.

1545
01:38:01,043 --> 01:38:03,045
- But I thought that...
- I don't care.

1546
01:38:03,211 --> 01:38:04,963
You're coming with me.
All right?

1547
01:38:06,548 --> 01:38:08,050
If that's
what's best for Rain.

1548
01:38:10,844 --> 01:38:12,846
Andy, I have
a new directive for you.

1549
01:38:14,723 --> 01:38:16,349
Do what's best for us.

1550
01:38:19,936 --> 01:38:20,937
Done.

1551
01:38:22,314 --> 01:38:23,315
Good.

1552
01:38:29,404 --> 01:38:31,323
[cryo-fuel hissing]

1553
01:38:36,995 --> 01:38:37,996
[alarm chiming]

1554
01:38:43,543 --> 01:38:44,544
No.

1555
01:38:46,630 --> 01:38:47,881
[grunting]

1556
01:38:48,215 --> 01:38:50,050
[gasps] Kay. Kay.

1557
01:38:51,093 --> 01:38:52,177
What's wrong?

1558
01:38:53,929 --> 01:38:55,222
- [squelching]
- Oh, no, no.

1559
01:38:55,514 --> 01:38:56,598
[yells in agony]

1560
01:38:57,182 --> 01:38:58,183
[♪ Tense music playing]

1561
01:38:59,101 --> 01:39:02,354
[Kay screaming]

1562
01:39:08,026 --> 01:39:09,486
[screaming]

1563
01:39:10,487 --> 01:39:11,655
[squelching]

1564
01:39:11,822 --> 01:39:12,823
[gasping]

1565
01:39:12,989 --> 01:39:14,032
[screaming]

1566
01:39:25,085 --> 01:39:27,254
Get it away from me.

1567
01:39:32,134 --> 01:39:33,218
[wailing]

1568
01:39:45,981 --> 01:39:47,065
[grunts]

1569
01:39:47,732 --> 01:39:49,025
[sizzling]

1570
01:39:52,863 --> 01:39:53,864
[grunting]

1571
01:40:07,586 --> 01:40:09,379
- [gasps softly]
- [baby cooing]

1572
01:40:22,559 --> 01:40:24,144
[engine powers down]

1573
01:40:34,738 --> 01:40:35,822
[gasps]

1574
01:40:35,906 --> 01:40:37,407
[alarm blaring]

1575
01:40:47,000 --> 01:40:48,001
[grunts]

1576
01:41:50,897 --> 01:41:52,107
[softly] Oh, my God.

1577
01:41:57,821 --> 01:41:59,281
[♪ Eerie music playing]

1578
01:42:13,044 --> 01:42:14,504
[electricity crackling]

1579
01:42:14,587 --> 01:42:15,880
[Kay groaning weakly]

1580
01:42:19,592 --> 01:42:21,344
[cryo-pod whirring]

1581
01:42:36,526 --> 01:42:38,528
- [gasping softly]
- [♪ tense music intensifies]

1582
01:42:45,201 --> 01:42:46,202
[♪ Music stops]

1583
01:42:46,286 --> 01:42:47,579
[alarm blaring faintly]

1584
01:42:47,662 --> 01:42:48,788
[whimpering]

1585
01:42:48,872 --> 01:42:50,749
[footsteps thudding]

1586
01:42:51,833 --> 01:42:55,086
[metal thudding]

1587
01:43:01,217 --> 01:43:02,719
[bones cracking]

1588
01:43:09,893 --> 01:43:11,227
- [snarling]
- [gasps]

1589
01:43:11,770 --> 01:43:13,355
[Kay screaming]

1590
01:43:13,438 --> 01:43:14,647
- [♪ Tense music resumes]
- [gasps]

1591
01:43:16,232 --> 01:43:17,233
[Rain] Kay.

1592
01:43:18,693 --> 01:43:20,111
[crying]

1593
01:43:30,747 --> 01:43:32,749
No. Please, please.

1594
01:43:39,172 --> 01:43:41,466
- [sniffing]
- [Kay sobbing]

1595
01:43:46,304 --> 01:43:47,639
[hissing]

1596
01:43:48,431 --> 01:43:49,682
[Kay wailing]

1597
01:43:56,022 --> 01:43:57,023
[Andy whimpering]

1598
01:43:57,982 --> 01:43:59,734
[Rain] Andy! Andy!

1599
01:44:01,611 --> 01:44:02,737
No, no, no.

1600
01:44:03,196 --> 01:44:05,448
Rain. Rain. Help her.

1601
01:44:11,621 --> 01:44:12,622
[coughs]

1602
01:44:21,881 --> 01:44:23,883
- [alarm continues blaring]
- [♪ tense music continues]

1603
01:44:26,094 --> 01:44:27,554
[flesh squelching]

1604
01:44:30,056 --> 01:44:31,057
[gasping]

1605
01:44:34,477 --> 01:44:36,146
[clicking]

1606
01:44:38,440 --> 01:44:39,441
[whimpers]

1607
01:44:42,819 --> 01:44:44,696
No! [screams]

1608
01:44:46,406 --> 01:44:47,407
No!

1609
01:44:47,782 --> 01:44:48,825
[snarling]

1610
01:44:50,493 --> 01:44:51,661
[grunts]

1611
01:44:53,830 --> 01:44:54,914
[grunting]

1612
01:44:59,836 --> 01:45:00,837
[coughs]

1613
01:45:01,754 --> 01:45:03,381
Andy! Come on!

1614
01:45:05,925 --> 01:45:07,135
Please get up!

1615
01:45:09,596 --> 01:45:10,680
[grunts]

1616
01:45:14,058 --> 01:45:15,059
[coughs]

1617
01:45:15,685 --> 01:45:16,686
No!

1618
01:45:20,815 --> 01:45:22,066
Come on!

1619
01:45:24,486 --> 01:45:25,612
[wheezing]

1620
01:46:04,984 --> 01:46:06,194
[wheezing heavily]

1621
01:46:07,737 --> 01:46:08,738
[suit chimes]

1622
01:46:08,821 --> 01:46:09,948
[oxygen hissing]

1623
01:46:12,450 --> 01:46:13,451
[breathes deeply]

1624
01:46:14,911 --> 01:46:16,704
[doors creaking]

1625
01:46:29,551 --> 01:46:30,718
[roars]

1626
01:46:46,442 --> 01:46:49,279
"Manual Cargo Release.
Pull the four levers."

1627
01:46:49,737 --> 01:46:52,949
Okay. Yes.
The four levers. Okay.

1628
01:47:01,040 --> 01:47:02,041
One.

1629
01:47:03,751 --> 01:47:04,752
Two.

1630
01:47:13,761 --> 01:47:15,054
[rope whirring]

1631
01:47:15,138 --> 01:47:16,347
[panting]

1632
01:47:23,521 --> 01:47:24,856
[machinery cranking]

1633
01:47:27,817 --> 01:47:28,818
Three.

1634
01:47:42,206 --> 01:47:43,499
[grunts]

1635
01:47:56,554 --> 01:47:58,473
[automated voice]
<i>Pull up. Pull up.</i>

1636
01:47:59,015 --> 01:48:00,308
[breathing laboriously]

1637
01:48:10,026 --> 01:48:11,152
[sizzling]

1638
01:48:20,870 --> 01:48:22,205
[shrieking]

1639
01:48:23,122 --> 01:48:24,290
[Rain grunts]

1640
01:48:34,634 --> 01:48:36,010
[air whooshing]

1641
01:48:47,897 --> 01:48:49,190
[breathing deeply]

1642
01:49:04,163 --> 01:49:05,164
- [screeching]
- [Rain gasps]

1643
01:49:06,499 --> 01:49:08,626
[Rain screaming]

1644
01:49:13,423 --> 01:49:14,465
[Rain whimpering]

1645
01:49:29,814 --> 01:49:31,107
[helmet thuds]

1646
01:49:36,279 --> 01:49:38,114
[over helmet]
<i>Die, motherfucker!</i>

1647
01:49:41,325 --> 01:49:43,327
[♪ Triumphant music playing]

1648
01:50:37,799 --> 01:50:39,383
[♪ Solemn music playing]

1649
01:50:58,402 --> 01:50:59,737
I'll fix you.

1650
01:51:15,878 --> 01:51:16,963
[Rain] <i>This is the cryo-log</i>

1651
01:51:17,046 --> 01:51:18,923
<i>for the mining hauler</i>
Corbelan.

1652
01:51:20,633 --> 01:51:22,593
<i>I set course
to the Yvaga system</i>

1653
01:51:22,677 --> 01:51:24,720
<i>without knowing
if I'll ever reach it,</i>

1654
01:51:24,887 --> 01:51:26,889
<i>or what fate is to find me.</i>

1655
01:51:28,015 --> 01:51:31,269
<i>But whatever comes,
I'll face it.</i>

1656
01:51:32,603 --> 01:51:33,938
<i>This is Rain Carradine,</i>

1657
01:51:34,105 --> 01:51:35,648
<i>last survivor
of the</i> Corbelan...

1658
01:51:36,232 --> 01:51:37,400
<i>signing off</i>

1659
01:51:38,442 --> 01:51:39,652
[♪ music soars]

1660
01:51:48,369 --> 01:51:49,370
[♪ Music fades]

1661
01:51:59,505 --> 01:52:01,507
[♪ Tense music playing]

1662
01:53:08,115 --> 01:53:10,159
[♪ Suspenseful music playing]

1663
01:58:48,747 --> 01:58:49,748
[♪ Music fades]

